{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786606267123,"sessionID":"ses_005f8753effeWyZ221Ua5lmfEm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_61RWxZRWA8Mg4SXRN1Zl5512","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/spec.md","offset":205,"limit":90},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n205: \n206: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n207: ## PHASE DOCUMENTATION MAP\n208: \n209: > This spec uses phased decomposition. Each phase is an independently executable child spec folder. Phases 001-002 are the read-only research inputs; phases 003-017 are the original implementation program. All implementation details (plan, tasks, checklist, decisions, continuity) live inside the phase children; the architecture ADR + the 178-row rec ledger live in 004. Phases 021-032 are the remediation tree for the 166 findings recorded in `016-whole-system-gate/review/`. Later direct children record follow-on hardening, review, and executor work. The root-level [`033-dispositions.md`](033-dispositions.md) is the review-disposition artifact; it is not phase `033-identity-and-lock-ownership-hardening/`.\n210: >\n211: > **Map maintenance:** folder coverage comes from the live direct-child census (`spec.md` or `description.json`), while each status is copied from that child's `graph-metadata.json` `derived.status`. `Metadata pending` means the qualifying child has no graph metadata yet; it is not an inferred execution status.\n212: \n213: | Phase | Folder | Focus | Status |\n214: |-------|--------|-------|--------|\n215: | 001 | 001-deep-loop-market-research/ | Market/landscape research + 8 ranked recs (read-only input) | Complete |\n216: | 002 | 002-deep-loop-effectiveness-and-fanout/ | 59 runtime recs + fan-out finding + 111 per-mode recs (read-only input) | Complete |\n217: | 003 | 003-baseline-taxonomy-and-state-census/ | Pinned BASE, normalized taxonomy, full state census | Complete |\n218: | 004 | 004-architecture-coverage-and-transition-contract/ | Architecture ADR + bijective 178-row ledger + transition contract (parent) | Planned |\n219: | 005 | 005-fanout-live-tools-unblock/ | Early backward-compatible live-tools fan-out unblock | Complete |\n220: | 006 | 006-transition-authorized-ledger-core/ | Event envelope + typed ledger + replay fingerprints + auth gateway (parent) | Planned |\n221: | 007 | 007-shared-evidence-and-control-services/ | Receipts, sealed artifacts, adjudication, budgets, gauges, locks (parent) | Planned |\n222: | 008 | 008-compatibility-shadow-and-rollback-bridge/ | Adapters + shadow parity + state classification + rollback (parent) | Planned |\n223: | 009 | 009-fanout-fanin-durable-orchestration/ | Durable fan-out/fan-in on the ledger (parent) | Planned |\n224: | 010 | 010-novelty-claims-continuity-and-projections/ | Novelty + contradiction + claim continuity + projections (parent) | Planned |\n225: | 011 | 011-convergence-termination-and-health/ | Termination + cycle detection + health/degeneration (parent) | Planned |\n226: | 012 | 012-shared-mode-contracts-and-fixtures/ | Shared mode contracts + write-set conflict graph (parent) | Planned |\n227: | 013 | 013-mode-and-lane-migrations/ | The eight per-mode migrations (parent ×8, each fractal) | In Progress |\n228: | 014 | 014-staged-state-migration-and-authority-cutover/ | Per-mode authority cutover + rollback window (parent) | Planned |\n229: | 015 | 015-legacy-writer-retirement/ | Gated legacy-writer removal; archival readers retained | Planned |\n230: | 016 | 016-whole-system-gate/ | Whole-system gate on the frozen SHA | Planned |\n231: | 017 | 017-integrate-latest-and-closeout/ | Integrate latest, rerun gate, reconcile, close out | Planned |\n232: | 018 | 018-drift-census-and-plan-revalidation/ | Drift census: revalidate phases 003-017 against current HEAD before execution | In Progress |\n233: | 019 | 019-runtime-code-readmes/ | Code READMEs for every source folder in the deep-loop runtime (sk-doc create-readme standard) | Complete |\n234: | 020 | 020-sk-code-opencode-alignment/ | Align the deep-loop runtime code with the sk-code code-opencode surface conventions (behavior-preserving) | Complete |\n235: | 021 | 021-completion-evidence-reconcile/ | Blocker 4: reconcile migration-program completion claims against the current suites; bound the review manifest and recursive validation | In Progress |\n236: | 022 | 022-shadow-parity-independent-derivation/ | Blocker 1: rebuild six shadow-parity harnesses so both sides derive independently | In Progress |\n237: | 023 | 023-legacy-compat-event-vocabulary/ | Blocker 2: full upcaster coverage for the six live event vocabularies | Complete |\n238: | 024 | 024-durable-write-boundaries/ | Blocker 3: gateway-only mutation with fencing at the append boundary; the concurrent-write family | In Progress |\n239: | 025 | 025-artifact-certificate-binding/ | Bind sealed artifacts and certificates to the semantic identity they certify | In Progress |\n240: | 026 | 026-alignment-coverage-integrity/ | Make alignment coverage, seal state and lane identity provable, including the three §5 residuals | Complete |\n241: | 027 | 027-mode-gate-and-contract-binding/ | Close the readiness-gate, rollback-switch and mode-contract conformance boundaries | Complete |\n242: | 028 | 028-fanout-dispatch-integrity/ | Evidence-derived fan-out fulfillment, durable provenance, uniform containment, safe sink | In Progress |\n243: | 029 | 029-improvement-promotion-authority/ | Bind promotion, rollback and council persistence to authenticated receipts and authorized roots | In Progress |\n244: | 030 | 030-runtime-mirror-and-routing-parity/ | Make runtime-mirror and routing parity gates compare what actually differs | In Progress |\n245: | 031 | 031-silent-failure-and-harness-repair/ | Make invalid input fail loudly; repair the harnesses and playbooks that produce evidence | In Progress |\n246: | 032 | 032-docs-drift-and-p2-batch/ | Documentation and registry drift plus the complete P2 backlog; runs last | In Progress |\n247: | 033 | 033-identity-and-lock-ownership-hardening/ | Identity and lock ownership hardening; distinct from root `033-dispositions.md` | Complete |\n248: | 035 | 035-cli-adapter-stress-and-playbooks/ | Planned stress-test and manual-playbook program for external CLI adapters | Planned |\n249: | 047 | 047-executor-wiring-and-parity/ | Executor wiring + fan-out parity group: cli-codex read-only leaf, cli-devin wiring, the executor/provider/model parity program, devin allowlist parity/prune (phase parent) | In Progress |\n250: | 048 | 048-write-containment-hardening/ | Fan-out write-containment guard hardening group: cli-codex containment, sibling-lineage scope, concurrent-writer safety (phase parent) | In Progress |\n251: | 049 | 049-deep-alignment-integrity/ | Deep-alignment loop integrity group: findings-registry seal state + contained multi-executor (phase parent) | In Progress |\n252: | 050 | 050-trustworthy-state-records/ | Trustworthy deep-loop state records: append-time stamps + stop-policy event-name fix | Complete |\n253: | 051 | 051-residual-finding-closeouts/ | Close residual findings carried from 022, 025, and 028 | In Progress |\n254: | 052 | 052-cli-devin-executor-repair/ | Repair workspace-trust and model-catalog drift in the cli-devin adapter | Complete |\n255: | 053 | 053-runtime-code-review/ | Deep-review artifact host for the runtime code audit | Planned |\n256: | 054 | 054-review-drift-remediation/ | Reconcile parent documentation and metadata drift | Metadata pending |\n257: | 055 | 055-rollback-candidate-hash-hardening/ | Track promoted-candidate-only rollback authority follow-up | Metadata pending |\n258: | 056 | 056-review-containment-exemption/ | Track the review containment exemption | Metadata pending |\n259: \n260: ### Phase Transition Rules\n261: - Each phase MUST pass `validate.sh` independently before the next phase begins.\n262: - Parent spec tracks aggregate progress via this map.\n263: - Use `/speckit:resume [parent-folder]/[NNN-phase]/` to resume a specific phase.\n264: - Run `validate.sh --recursive` on this parent to validate all phases as an integrated unit.\n265: \n266: ### Phase Handoff Criteria\n267: \n268: | From | To | Criteria | Verification |\n269: |------|-----|----------|--------------|\n270: | 002 | 003 | Research inputs complete and frozen; 178 recs available for the ledger | The three findings-registry files present and read-only |\n271: | 003 | 004 | BASE pinned; taxonomy normalized; state + schema + behavior baseline captured | Baseline artifacts keyed by BASE; extended packet-033 benchmark recorded |\n272: | 004 | 005-007 | Architecture ratified; 178-row bijective ledger frozen; transition/compat/cutover policy set | Single-disposition validator green; transition vocabulary + namespace published |\n273: | 006-007 | 008 | Ledger core + shared services land dark; legacy still authoritative | Auth gate rejects an unauthorized transition; dark-write parity smoke passes |\n274: | 008 | 009-011 | Adapters + shadow parity + rollback proven; no authority moved | Shadow parity green; a rollback drill restores legacy; in-flight state classified |\n275: | 009-011 | 012 | Durable fan-in + novelty/claims + convergence land on the ledger (dark) | Deterministic replay under the fingerprint; convergence inputs resolve |\n276: | 012 | 013 | Shared mode contracts frozen; write-set conflict graph emitted | Parallel-safe lane plan; deep-improvement-common ordered first |\n277: | 013 | 014 | Every mode migrated + shadow-parity green behind its mode gate | Per-mode gate checklists pass; sealed artifact/certificate emitted per mode |\n278: | 014 | 015 | Authority flipped per mode behind rollback windows + cutover certificates | Cutover certificate per mode; rollback drill green post-cutover |\n279: | 015 | 016 | Legacy writers removed after zero-use; archival readers retained | Zero-use telemetry; historical packets still read |\n280: | 016 | 017 | Whole-system gate green on the pre-integration SHA | `--all` behavior + mode + replay + degeneration parity vs 003 |\n281: | 021-024 | 014 | The four named cutover blockers are discharged: evidence reconciles (021), shadow parity can fail (022), live vocabularies migrate (023), the append boundary is fenced (024) | Per blocker: reinstated evidence cites test name + suite digest + SHA; a divergence injection fails the rebuilt parity harness; a captured real log replays with zero `blocked:unknown-legacy-record`; a superseded writer with an unexpired proof cannot append |\n282: | 021-032 | 017 | The whole remediation tree is Complete against the bounded child manifest | `validate.sh --recursive --strict` green over the declared 001-032 manifest; every one of the 166 register findings closed as fixed, REFUTED, ALREADY-FIXED, or dispositioned |\n283: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n\n(End of file - total 283 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n## PHASE DOCUMENTATION MAP\n\n> This spec uses phased decomposition. Each phase is an independently executable child spec folder. Phases 001-002 are the read-only research inputs; phases 003-017 are the original implementation program. All implementation details (plan, tasks, checklist, decisions, continuity) live inside the phase children; the architecture ADR + the 178-row rec ledger live in 004. Phases 021-032 are the remediation tree for the 166 findings recorded in `016-whole-system-gate/review/`. Later direct children record follow-on hardening, review, and executor work. The root-level [`033-dispositions.md`](033-dispositions.md) is the review-disposition artifact; it is not phase `033-identity-and-lock-ownership-hardening/`.\n>\n> **Map maintenance:** folder coverage comes from the live direct-child census (`spec.md` or `description.json`), while each status is copied from that child's `graph-metadata.json` `derived.status`. `Metadata pending` means the qualifying child has no graph metadata yet; it is not an inferred execution status.\n\n| Phase | Folder | Focus | Status |\n|-------|--------|-------|--------|\n| 001 | 001-deep-loop-market-research/ | Market/landscape research + 8 ranked recs (read-only input) | Complete |\n| 002 | 002-deep-loop-effectiveness-and-fanout/ | 59 runtime recs + fan-out finding + 111 per-mode recs (read-only input) | Complete |\n| 003 | 003-baseline-taxonomy-and-state-census/ | Pinned BASE, normalized taxonomy, full state census | Complete |\n| 004 | 004-architecture-coverage-and-transition-contract/ | Architecture ADR + bijective 178-row ledger + transition contract (parent) | Planned |\n| 005 | 005-fanout-live-tools-unblock/ | Early backward-compatible live-tools fan-out unblock | Complete |\n| 006 | 006-transition-authorized-ledger-core/ | Event envelope + typed ledger + replay fingerprints + auth gateway (parent) | Planned |\n| 007 | 007-shared-evidence-and-control-services/ | Receipts, sealed artifacts, adjudication, budgets, gauges, locks (parent) | Planned |\n| 008 | 008-compatibility-shadow-and-rollback-bridge/ | Adapters + shadow parity + state classification + rollback (parent) | Planned |\n| 009 | 009-fanout-fanin-durable-orchestration/ | Durable fan-out/fan-in on the ledger (parent) | Planned |\n| 010 | 010-novelty-claims-continuity-and-projections/ | Novelty + contradiction + claim continuity + projections (parent) | Planned |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/spec.md","text":"\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n## PHASE DOCUMENTATION MAP\n\n> This spec uses phased decomposition. Each phase is an independently executable child spec folder. Phases 001-002 are the read-only research inputs; phases 003-017 are the original implementation program. All implementation details (plan, tasks, checklist, decisions, continuity) live inside the phase children; the architecture ADR + the 178-row rec ledger live in 004. Phases 021-032 are the remediation tree for the 166 findings recorded in `016-whole-system-gate/review/`. Later direct children record follow-on hardening, review, and executor work. The root-level [`033-dispositions.md`](033-dispositions.md) is the review-disposition artifact; it is not phase `033-identity-and-lock-ownership-hardening/`.\n>\n> **Map maintenance:** folder coverage comes from the live direct-child census (`spec.md` or `description.json`), while each status is copied from that child's `graph-metadata.json` `derived.status`. `Metadata pending` means the qualifying child has no graph metadata yet; it is not an inferred execution status.\n\n| Phase | Folder | Focus | Status |\n|-------|--------|-------|--------|\n| 001 | 001-deep-loop-market-research/ | Market/landscape research + 8 ranked recs (read-only input) | Complete |\n| 002 | 002-deep-loop-effectiveness-and-fanout/ | 59 runtime recs + fan-out finding + 111 per-mode recs (read-only input) | Complete |\n| 003 | 003-baseline-taxonomy-and-state-census/ | Pinned BASE, normalized taxonomy, full state census | Complete |\n| 004 | 004-architecture-coverage-and-transition-contract/ | Architecture ADR + bijective 178-row ledger + transition contract (parent) | Planned |\n| 005 | 005-fanout-live-tools-unblock/ | Early backward-compatible live-tools fan-out unblock | Complete |\n| 006 | 006-transition-authorized-ledger-core/ | Event envelope + typed ledger + replay fingerprints + auth gateway (parent) | Planned |\n| 007 | 007-shared-evidence-and-control-services/ | Receipts, sealed artifacts, adjudication, budgets, gauges, locks (parent) | Planned |\n| 008 | 008-compatibility-shadow-and-rollback-bridge/ | Adapters + shadow parity + state classification + rollback (parent) | Planned |\n| 009 | 009-fanout-fanin-durable-orchestration/ | Durable fan-out/fan-in on the ledger (parent) | Planned |\n| 010 | 010-novelty-claims-continuity-and-projections/ | Novelty + contradiction + claim continuity + projections (parent) | Planned |\n| 011 | 011-convergence-termination-and-health/ | Termination + cycle detection + health/degeneration (parent) | Planned |\n| 012 | 012-shared-mode-contracts-and-fixtures/ | Shared mode contracts + write-set conflict graph (parent) | Planned |\n| 013 | 013-mode-and-lane-migrations/ | The eight per-mode migrations (parent ×8, each fractal) | In Progress |\n| 014 | 014-staged-state-migration-and-authority-cutover/ | Per-mode authority cutover + rollback window (parent) | Planned |\n| 015 | 015-legacy-writer-retirement/ | Gated legacy-writer removal; archival readers retained | Planned |\n| 016 | 016-whole-system-gate/ | Whole-system gate on the frozen SHA | Planned |\n| 017 | 017-integrate-latest-and-closeout/ | Integrate latest, rerun gate, reconcile, close out | Planned |\n| 018 | 018-drift-census-and-plan-revalidation/ | Drift census: revalidate phases 003-017 against current HEAD before execution | In Progress |\n| 019 | 019-runtime-code-readmes/ | Code READMEs for every source folder in the deep-loop runtime (sk-doc create-readme standard) | Complete |\n| 020 | 020-sk-code-opencode-alignment/ | Align the deep-loop runtime code with the sk-code code-opencode surface conventions (behavior-preserving) | Complete |\n| 021 | 021-completion-evidence-reconcile/ | Blocker 4: reconcile migration-program completion claims against the current suites; bound the review manifest and recursive validation | In Progress |\n| 022 | 022-shadow-parity-independent-derivation/ | Blocker 1: rebuild six shadow-parity harnesses so both sides derive independently | In Progress |\n| 023 | 023-legacy-compat-event-vocabulary/ | Blocker 2: full upcaster coverage for the six live event vocabularies | Complete |\n| 024 | 024-durable-write-boundaries/ | Blocker 3: gateway-only mutation with fencing at the append boundary; the concurrent-write family | In Progress |\n| 025 | 025-artifact-certificate-binding/ | Bind sealed artifacts and certificates to the semantic identity they certify | In Progress |\n| 026 | 026-alignment-coverage-integrity/ | Make alignment coverage, seal state and lane identity provable, including the three §5 residuals | Complete |\n| 027 | 027-mode-gate-and-contract-binding/ | Close the readiness-gate, rollback-switch and mode-contract conformance boundaries | Complete |\n| 028 | 028-fanout-dispatch-integrity/ | Evidence-derived fan-out fulfillment, durable provenance, uniform containment, safe sink | In Progress |\n| 029 | 029-improvement-promotion-authority/ | Bind promotion, rollback and council persistence to authenticated receipts and authorized roots | In Progress |\n| 030 | 030-runtime-mirror-and-routing-parity/ | Make runtime-mirror and routing parity gates compare what actually differs | In Progress |\n| 031 | 031-silent-failure-and-harness-repair/ | Make invalid input fail loudly; repair the harnesses and playbooks that produce evidence | In Progress |\n| 032 | 032-docs-drift-and-p2-batch/ | Documentation and registry drift plus the complete P2 backlog; runs last | In Progress |\n| 033 | 033-identity-and-lock-ownership-hardening/ | Identity and lock ownership hardening; distinct from root `033-dispositions.md` | Complete |\n| 035 | 035-cli-adapter-stress-and-playbooks/ | Planned stress-test and manual-playbook program for external CLI adapters | Planned |\n| 047 | 047-executor-wiring-and-parity/ | Executor wiring + fan-out parity group: cli-codex read-only leaf, cli-devin wiring, the executor/provider/model parity program, devin allowlist parity/prune (phase parent) | In Progress |\n| 048 | 048-write-containment-hardening/ | Fan-out write-containment guard hardening group: cli-codex containment, sibling-lineage scope, concurrent-writer safety (phase parent) | In Progress |\n| 049 | 049-deep-alignment-integrity/ | Deep-alignment loop integrity group: findings-registry seal state + contained multi-executor (phase parent) | In Progress |\n| 050 | 050-trustworthy-state-records/ | Trustworthy deep-loop state records: append-time stamps + stop-policy event-name fix | Complete |\n| 051 | 051-residual-finding-closeouts/ | Close residual findings carried from 022, 025, and 028 | In Progress |\n| 052 | 052-cli-devin-executor-repair/ | Repair workspace-trust and model-catalog drift in the cli-devin adapter | Complete |\n| 053 | 053-runtime-code-review/ | Deep-review artifact host for the runtime code audit | Planned |\n| 054 | 054-review-drift-remediation/ | Reconcile parent documentation and metadata drift | Metadata pending |\n| 055 | 055-rollback-candidate-hash-hardening/ | Track promoted-candidate-only rollback authority follow-up | Metadata pending |\n| 056 | 056-review-containment-exemption/ | Track the review containment exemption | Metadata pending |\n\n### Phase Transition Rules\n- Each phase MUST pass `validate.sh` independently before the next phase begins.\n- Parent spec tracks aggregate progress via this map.\n- Use `/speckit:resume [parent-folder]/[NNN-phase]/` to resume a specific phase.\n- Run `validate.sh --recursive` on this parent to validate all phases as an integrated unit.\n\n### Phase Handoff Criteria\n\n| From | To | Criteria | Verification |\n|------|-----|----------|--------------|\n| 002 | 003 | Research inputs complete and frozen; 178 recs available for the ledger | The three findings-registry files present and read-only |\n| 003 | 004 | BASE pinned; taxonomy normalized; state + schema + behavior baseline captured | Baseline artifacts keyed by BASE; extended packet-033 benchmark recorded |\n| 004 | 005-007 | Architecture ratified; 178-row bijective ledger frozen; transition/compat/cutover policy set | Single-disposition validator green; transition vocabulary + namespace published |\n| 006-007 | 008 | Ledger core + shared services land dark; legacy still authoritative | Auth gate rejects an unauthorized transition; dark-write parity smoke passes |\n| 008 | 009-011 | Adapters + shadow parity + rollback proven; no authority moved | Shadow parity green; a rollback drill restores legacy; in-flight state classified |\n| 009-011 | 012 | Durable fan-in + novelty/claims + convergence land on the ledger (dark) | Deterministic replay under the fingerprint; convergence inputs resolve |\n| 012 | 013 | Shared mode contracts frozen; write-set conflict graph emitted | Parallel-safe lane plan; deep-improvement-common ordered first |\n| 013 | 014 | Every mode migrated + shadow-parity green behind its mode gate | Per-mode gate checklists pass; sealed artifact/certificate emitted per mode |\n| 014 | 015 | Authority flipped per mode behind rollback windows + cutover certificates | Cutover certificate per mode; rollback drill green post-cutover |\n| 015 | 016 | Legacy writers removed after zero-use; archival readers retained | Zero-use telemetry; historical packets still read |\n| 016 | 017 | Whole-system gate green on the pre-integration SHA | `--all` behavior + mode + replay + degeneration parity vs 003 |\n| 021-024 | 014 | The four named cutover blockers are discharged: evidence reconciles (021), shadow parity can fail (022), live vocabularies migrate (023), the append boundary is fenced (024) | Per blocker: reinstated evidence cites test name + suite digest + SHA; a divergence injection fails the rebuilt parity harness; a captured real log replays with zero `blocked:unknown-legacy-record`; a superseded writer with an unexpired proof cannot append |\n| 021-032 | 017 | The whole remediation tree is Complete against the bounded child manifest | `validate.sh --recursive --strict` green over the declared 001-032 manifest; every one of the 166 register findings closed as fixed, REFUTED, ALREADY-FIXED, or dispositioned |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-map -->","lineStart":205,"lineEnd":283,"totalLines":283,"truncated":false}},"title":"specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/spec.md","time":{"start":1786606267113,"end":1786606267121}},"id":"prt_ffa082923001W4YFrXvL5oKMAt","sessionID":"ses_005f8753effeWyZ221Ua5lmfEm","messageID":"msg_ffa081b1f001jYJTD17KDi2ITp"}}
